\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Ordinary and generalized zero modes}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{Over a field of characteristic different from #{2}, let the
positive eigenspace have basis #{u_1,u_2} and the negative
eigenspace have basis #{w}. Let #{Au_1=w}, #{Au_2=0} and
#{Aw=0}. This operator is odd and #{A^2=0}. Its kernel is
spanned by #{u_2,w} and has index zero. Its generalized kernel
is the whole space and has index #{1}, as in \ref{fdip-013P}.
The vector #{w} lies in both the image and the kernel, so the
hypothesis of \ref{fdip-013Q} fails.}

\p{In positive even dimension the covariant centered operator
#{D_{a,U}} is skew-adjoint by \ref{fdip-009P} and odd for the
volume grading #{C} of \ref{fdip-009X}. An invertible generator
exchanges the two ambient eigenspaces. By \ref{fdip-013Q}, the
kernel therefore has index zero for every unitary connection.
At trivial links \ref{fdip-009Q} counts all zero modes, and
half lie in each eigenspace of #{C}.}
